description: |
  The ``junit`` report now writes the ``time`` attribute for a result
  whose duration was measured as zero. The attribute used to be left out
  whenever the whole seconds came out as zero, so a quick test showed the
  attribute or not depending on whether it happened to cross the one
  second mark.

  A ``start-time`` or ``end-time`` written without a timezone is read as
  UTC and written back with the ``+00:00`` offset. The format was always
  documented as a full ISO 8601 date and time, so a value that followed
  the documentation is unchanged; a value that left the offset out now
  gains it.
